From 0562c23e5718fac265132a5347eaa1db8e20a742 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 12:51:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rtrafd: detach rt_bound's watcher from the pipe - the v2.8.6
 live-freeze regression

The rt_bound() popen timeout wrapper (2026-08-26 audit remediation) let its
watcher subshell - and the sleep it forks, which `kill $_w` never reaches -
inherit the pipe's write fd. A popen reader gets EOF only when the last holder
of that fd closes it, so a tmctl that answered in milliseconds still cost the
collector the FULL timeout of blocked fgets(). With HW classful QoS on, that is
7 queues x 3 s per 4 s class poll plus 6 s per ping-probe cycle: the
single-threaded collector spent ~27 s blocked per loop pass and live.json was
rewritten once per pass instead of 10x/s. Field symptom (v2.8.6/v2.8.7 metal,
2026-08-27): Traffic Analyzer live metrics flatline, lurching forward every
~20-30 s.

Confirmed on RT-BE96U hardware: live.json mtime frozen 22 s then a burst; the
shipped wrapper measured 3 s and the fixed one 0 s for an instant child on the
router's own busybox 1.25.1. The audit's metal check verified rtrafd CPU -
which stayed flat, correctly, because the daemon was blocked, not spinning.

Fix: redirect the watcher to /dev/null before it forks, so nothing but the
bounded command holds the pipe. Popen-harness measured: fast path
3.008 s -> 0.005 s; a hung child is still killed at the deadline. Host ring
harness still 9/9.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/rtrafd/rtrafd.c | 15 +++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/release/src/router/rtrafd/rtrafd.c b/release/src/router/rtrafd/rtrafd.c
index 67719b4027..cda65d5f79 100644
--- a/release/src/router/rtrafd/rtrafd.c
+++ b/release/src/router/rtrafd/rtrafd.c
@@ -947,11 +947,22 @@ static void poll_ifaces(const char *wanif)
  * whole collector - WAN sampling, live.json, history rollover - stops with it.
  * busybox has no `timeout` applet (rmcpd records the same) and popen() hands
  * back no pid to kill, so the ceiling goes inside the command: run it in the
- * background, arm a killer, take whichever finishes first. */
+ * background, arm a killer, take whichever finishes first.
+ *
+ * The watcher MUST NOT inherit the pipe (v2.8.6 field regression): a popen
+ * reader gets EOF only when every holder of the write fd has closed it, and
+ * the watcher subshell - and the sleep it forks, which `kill $_w` does not
+ * reach - held a copy for the full timeout. So a tmctl that answered in
+ * milliseconds still cost the caller `secs` seconds of fgets(): 7 queues x 3 s
+ * every 4 s class poll froze the whole collector, live.json included, which
+ * the page renders as flatlined metrics that lurch forward every ~20 s.
+ * Redirecting the watcher to /dev/null before it forks is the entire fix;
+ * measured in the popen harness: 3.008 s -> 0.005 s fast path, hung child
+ * still killed at `secs`. */
 static void rt_bound(char *out, size_t n, const char *cmd, int secs)
 {
 	snprintf(out, n,
-	         "{ %s; } & _c=$!; { sleep %d; kill -9 $_c 2>/dev/null; } & _w=$!; "
+	         "{ %s; } & _c=$!; { sleep %d; kill -9 $_c 2>/dev/null; } >/dev/null 2>&1 & _w=$!; "
 	         "wait $_c 2>/dev/null; kill $_w 2>/dev/null",
 	         cmd, secs);
 }
